WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.217
This is Auditlock, the escrow workspace for security audit delivery. On the left is my

00:00:05.217 --> 00:00:10.373
local test operator. On the right is the actual deployed app. I am accepting a funded

00:00:10.373 --> 00:00:12.982
test agreement with a fresh auditor wallet.

00:00:13.982 --> 00:00:19.280
The app's new audit form fixes the agreement before work starts. This form demonstration

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.290
is separate from the signed SDK test transactions.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:28.350
I enter a repository, its full commit hash, and the invited auditor wallet. Each

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:33.789
milestone has its own funded amount and acceptance criteria. The browser form is real,

00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:36.572
but I am not signing a customer wallet here.

00:00:43.368 --> 00:00:48.466
The first attempt hits StudioNet's hourly request limit before report submission. Two

00:00:48.466 --> 00:00:53.385
transactions finalized. This failure is retained in the public evidence; it is not

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:55.185
presented as a completed test.

00:00:56.279 --> 00:01:01.130
I reduced unnecessary app polling and added request-limit backoff. Now I start a new

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:06.154
run. The script creates fresh test wallets and retains them in memory while waiting for

00:01:06.154 --> 00:01:11.005
the service quota to recover. Confirmation waits are omitted between recorded clips.

00:01:18.426 --> 00:01:23.665
I confirm the owner transaction. It deposits point zero one test GEN into the real

00:01:23.665 --> 00:01:28.393
GenLayer contract, allocated across the report and remediation milestones.

00:01:33.922 --> 00:01:39.097
The separate auditor signs acceptance of the frozen scope and settlement rules. The

00:01:39.097 --> 00:01:42.340
contract, not this console, records that acceptance.

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:52.369
I select the new run in the actual live registry. Its contract record fixes the

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:58.027
repository, full code revision, two milestone allocations, and acceptance criteria. The

00:01:58.027 --> 00:02:00.889
owner and auditor are distinct test wallets.

00:02:07.241 --> 00:02:11.729
I record a synthetic audit report and a public source snapshot at the exact code

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:16.443
revision. The report is a test fixture; its submission and content hash are real on-

00:02:16.443 --> 00:02:17.228
chain records.

00:02:22.978 --> 00:02:27.960
The auditor submits the first milestone for review. This starts the owner's forty-eight-

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.206
hour challenge window.

00:02:37.037 --> 00:02:42.469
In the live app I inspect the new engagement, its frozen commit, acceptance criteria,

00:02:42.469 --> 00:02:47.581
and recorded report. Evidence is attributed to its submitting wallet. A snapshot

00:02:47.581 --> 00:02:50.969
preserves content; it does not certify code security.

00:02:57.594 --> 00:03:02.892
The protocol owner accepts the report. Only its point zero zero seven GEN allocation

00:03:02.892 --> 00:03:07.686
becomes the auditor's withdrawal credit. The retest allocation stays locked.

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:17.707
The exhibit contains both the auditor's attributed statement and the source text

00:03:17.707 --> 00:03:22.158
retrieved at submission. Its content digest fixes that record for later review; it is

00:03:22.158 --> 00:03:24.881
not a claim that the code has been audited securely.

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:34.596
For the second milestone I deliberately submit a report admitting that neither required

00:03:34.596 --> 00:03:39.256
remediation check was performed. This provides a concrete unmet deliverable for the live

00:03:39.256 --> 00:03:40.051
consensus test.

00:03:44.797 --> 00:03:49.560
The auditor submits that incomplete retest document. The test concerns the agreed

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:53.029
deliverable, not whether the referenced protocol is secure.

00:03:57.225 --> 00:04:02.327
The owner challenges criterion C one, which requires an outcome for both findings. The

00:04:02.327 --> 00:04:06.657
challenge identifies exactly what the submitted report failed to provide.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:15.862
The owner records a comparison between the frozen criterion and the auditor's own

00:04:15.862 --> 00:04:19.393
admission. Both sides' evidence remains available to GenLayer.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:29.578
The owner signs readiness for assessment. One signature alone cannot shorten the

00:04:29.578 --> 00:04:30.563
response period.

00:04:35.104 --> 00:04:40.129
The auditor also signs readiness. Both parties have now explicitly agreed to proceed

00:04:40.129 --> 00:04:42.342
before the full response window ends.

00:04:45.402 --> 00:04:50.770
A third test wallet requests assessment. GenLayer validators independently evaluate the

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:55.644
frozen agreement and recorded evidence. The console does not choose the ruling.

00:05:04.796 --> 00:05:09.978
The live app shows the actual accepted criterion result and explanation. Deterministic

00:05:09.978 --> 00:05:14.859
contract rules turn that result into the milestone's payment or refund. This is a

00:05:14.859 --> 00:05:17.873
delivery judgment, never a security certification.

00:05:32.046 --> 00:05:37.008
The owner withdraws its credit. The test checks the finalized child transfer and the

00:05:37.008 --> 00:05:39.194
owner's actual wallet balance change.

00:05:46.146 --> 00:05:51.312
The auditor separately withdraws its earned report payment. The test verifies the exact

00:05:51.312 --> 00:05:54.579
balance increase, not just a successful parent receipt.

00:06:00.692 --> 00:06:05.620
The app exposes the agreed review windows, criterion-based settlement, and timeout

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:10.729
recovery. This walkthrough uses StudioNet test GEN and synthetic report fixtures. The

00:06:10.729 --> 00:06:15.959
transactions, consensus judgment, and transfers were executed on the real test network.

00:06:15.959 --> 00:06:18.123
Public receipts accompany the video.

00:06:23.188 --> 00:06:28.173
I fund a separate point zero zero one GEN engagement to test cancellation before auditor

00:06:28.173 --> 00:06:28.796
acceptance.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:41.931
The owner cancels the unaccepted engagement. Its full deposit becomes a refund credit

00:06:41.931 --> 00:06:44.123
without affecting the completed audit.

00:06:49.582 --> 00:06:54.638
The owner withdraws that cancellation refund. Again the test verifies both successful

00:06:54.638 --> 00:06:57.910
transfer finality and the actual wallet balance change.

00:07:03.639 --> 00:07:08.810
The activity tab reconstructs this agreement's funding, acceptance, signed exhibits,

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:14.042
submissions, challenge, and consensus settlement. These events come from the contract

00:07:14.042 --> 00:07:17.920
record for the new run, not a fabricated demonstration history.

00:07:24.007 --> 00:07:29.038
The completed run contains seventeen finalized parent transactions and three finalized

00:07:29.038 --> 00:07:34.128
withdrawal transfers. Every assertion passed, including exact payouts and contract-wide

00:07:34.128 --> 00:07:38.925
accounting conservation. The earlier interrupted fixture remains visible under its

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:42.728
original deadline. No result has been replaced with a simulation.
